<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
                      http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.29.xsd"
    objectQuotingStrategy="QUOTE_ONLY_RESERVED_WORDS">

    <!-- How long the drops may wait for their lock; a Liquibase parameter of the same name overrides it. -->
    <property name="submissionIndexLockTimeout" value="30s"/>

    <!--
      Drops two indexes on data_submission that no query can use, while every upload maintains them.

      - idx_ds_form_data_gin, a GIN on form_data: 46-48 MB at 57 k submissions, about 0.7 GB at a million. A GIN
        serves only the jsonb operators @>, ?, ?|, ?&, @? and @@, and none of them appears in the application's
        native SQL, JPQL or criteria (the generic query builds =, <>, <, >, IN, LIKE and IS NULL on attributes),
        in the integrity checks or the pivot SQL (they call jsonb_each and jsonb_path_query, which no index
        serves), or in a database function, view or trigger (none names data_submission on the staging clone).
        Production never scanned it.
      - idx_ds_serial_number, a plain btree on serial_number: a duplicate of the unique uk_data_submission_serial,
        which serves every serial_number lookup once it is gone (the planner picks either today).

      Kept: the primary key, uk_data_submission_uid, uk_data_submission_serial and idx_ds_form_assignment, and two
      that production never scanned but a live route would use: the planner picks idx_ds_orgunit and
      idx_ds_active_form_assignment for the generic read surface (/objects, /query) when an admin filters by org
      unit or by form. They go when that surface retires.

      A plain DROP INDEX holds an ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock on data_submission for a moment, so lock_timeout makes the
      deploy fail visibly instead of waiting behind a long read or upload. The rollback recreates each index with
      the definition changeset 2025-09-01 gave it (the staging clone has exactly these); rebuilding the GIN blocks
      uploads while it runs.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20261125-03-drop-unused-submission-indexes" author="datarun">
        <sql>SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '${submissionIndexLockTimeout}'</sql>
        <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS idx_ds_form_data_gin</sql>
        <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS idx_ds_serial_number</sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql>SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '${submissionIndexLockTimeout}'</sql>
            <sql>CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ds_form_data_gin ON data_submission USING gin (form_data)</sql>
            <sql>CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ds_serial_number ON data_submission USING btree (serial_number)</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
